Currently, you can specify in the .nethackrc file what class you want to
play, or specify it as random--at which point it will pick from the whole
list.  I like the idea of having a random char, but I'd like to exclude
certain choices (ie., I've ascended A and B, so I'd rather play other
classes; also, I'm not sure I want to play S yet, since I'd have to go
through all the bother of learning the names of items again...:-)  So, I'd
like a patch which adds {class/race/align}_exceptions (gender doesn't need
an exception, obviously), which would remove the listed items from the
random list.

Does such a patch exist somewhere?  If not, any intrepid source-divers want
to produce one?  (I would, but I have a serious lack of free time these
days...I'm lucky to get any NH in at all...*sigh*)



